\details{
The module shows a protein or nucleic-acid structure from
\code{\link[=read_structure]{read_structure()}} in an interactive 3D viewer (see \code{\link[=structureViewer]{structureViewer()}}).
Changing the style, colours or highlighted residues restyles the structure in
place, so the view you have rotated to is kept.

This module is \strong{not a plotly figure}: plotly has no molecular graphics, so
it uses the NGL viewer (NGLVieweR) instead. It therefore has no Figure Builder
